# Code Quality

Apply when validating, fixing, or writing TypeScript:

## TypeScript

- Never use `any`. Use specific types or named interfaces.
- Type refs exactly; extend `Window` inline for vendor APIs.
- Cast Three.js materials to concrete types before accessing uniforms.

## Lint & Build

- Must pass `npm run lint` and `npm run build` with zero errors before committing.
- Prefix unused vars with `_`; never use `@ts-nocheck`.
- Use `catch {}` (no binding) for intentional suppression, or log and re-throw.
- Only `console.error`/`console.warn` for unrecoverable browser-API failures.
- Include every referenced variable in hook dependency arrays.
- Async/await only — never `.then()/.catch()` chains.

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const ref = useRef<any>(null);
} catch (e) {}

// ✅ GOOD
const ref = useRef<THREE.Mesh>(null);
} catch {
  // intentional — AudioContext not supported
}
```

